"lp": -3.099489549640566e-05, "top": [["C", -3.099489549640566e-05], ["c", -12.352858543395996]]}, {"t": "++", "lp": -0.0006918915896676481, "top": [["++", -0.0006918915896676481], ["XX", -7.321835994720459]]}, {"t": "**", "lp": -0.061359260231256485, "top": [["**", -0.061359260231256485], ["/", -2.9321086406707764]]}, {"t": " compiler", "lp": -0.03849486634135246, "top": [[" compiler", -0.03849486634135246], [" (", -3.3662002086639404]]}, {"t": " |", "lp": -0.24988588690757751, "top": [[" |", -0.24988588690757751], [" (", -1.749061942100525]]}, {"t": "\n", "lp": -0.15920449793338776, "top": [["\n", -0.15920449793338776], ["\n\n", -1.9161540269851685]]}, {"t": "|", "lp": -0.0006239572539925575, "top": [["|", -0.0006239572539925575], ["|-", -10.037376403808594]]}], "text": "# PKGBUILD build() Function: Step-by-Step Explanation\n\nLet me break down this `build()` function line by line.\n\n## The Setup\n\n```bash\nsource /opt/intel/oneapi/setvars.sh --force\n```\nThis loads the Intel oneAPI environment variables (compiler paths, library paths, etc.). The `--force` flag forces the environment to be set up even if it appears already configured. This is essential because we're compiling with Intel's `icx`/`icpx` compilers, not the default GCC.\n\n```bash\nset -e\n```\nThis makes the script exit immediately if any command returns a non-zero (error) status. A safety net so a failed command doesn't cascade into confusing errors.\n\n## The CMake Configuration\n\nNow the main `cmake` command. Let me flag each part:\n\n| Flag | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| `-S \"${srcdir}/llama.cpp\"` | **Source directory** \u2014 where the source code lives |\n| `-B \"${srcdir}/build\"` | **Build directory** \u2014 where build artifacts go (out-of-source build) |\n| `-G Ninja` | Use the **Ninja** build system (fast, efficient) instead of Make |\n| `-DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release` | Optimize build with performance flags (`-O3`, etc.) |\n| `-DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/usr` | Where files will be installed (standard system location) |\n| `-DCMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR=lib` | Install libraries to `lib/` (not `lib64/`) |\n| `-DCMAKE_C_COMPILER=icx` | Use Intel's **C** compiler |\n| `-DCMAKE_CXX_COMPILER=icpx` | Use Intel's **C++** compiler |\n|"}